    "message": "XspecT has been replaced by Xspec. The new framework maintains a similar fluent syntax but is built on a vastly superior, dependency-free architecture. It offers significantly better execution speed and new features, like semantic test data. Upgrading to Xspec involves several breaking changes, most notably heavier use of `Using` keyword for providing defaults.",
